{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "contract": "native-cli-option-domains",
  "comment": [
    "The accepted value set of every native CLI option whose contract is narrower",
    "than its scalar type, and every required option whose absence is reported as",
    "an invalid parameter rather than a usage error.",
    "",
    "This is the declaration the two CLIs agree on. rejectExit names the exit-code",
    "class the refusal carries: 'usage' (2) is what the Python parser reports for a",
    "type=/choices= rejection, and 'invalid_parameter' (3) is what its handler",
    "reports after parsing. tests/conformance/cli_contract_v2.json drives the same",
    "values through both executables; this file is what the native registry is",
    "pinned against, so a domain cannot be added, moved between classes, or dropped",
    "without the change showing up here."
  ],
